Enhancement: Make `copy` resume interrupted runs using a persistent progress ledger

The `copy` command now records the copy progress of each source snapshot in the
destination repository. When a copy run was interrupted, for example due to a
network failure, rerunning it skips snapshots that were already copied
completely, does not transfer their data again, and only finishes the remaining
snapshots. Snapshots created manually in the destination repository are left
untouched. The progress records can be inspected using `restic list copy-state`.

If the progress records cannot be written to the destination repository, the
`copy` command now fails instead of continuing without progress tracking.

